'''Ithia Paan''' was a [[Kel Dor]] [[Gender|female]] [[Jedi Knight]] of the [[Jedi Order]] during the [[High Republic Era]]. She served as a [[diplomat]] between the [[Jedi]] Order and the [[Baran Do Sages]]. In [[132 BBY]], she was briefed by Jedi Knight [[Yord Fandar]] on a [[Mission to Khofar|mission]] to the [[planet]] [[Khofar]] to locate the [[assassin]] [[Mae-ho Aniseya]] before she could [[Death|kill]] the secluded [[Jedi Master]] [[Kelnacca]]. She perished against the [[Sith]] practitioner known as "[[the Stranger]]" during the mission.

==Biography==
Ithia Paan was a [[Kel Dor]] [[Jedi Knight]] of the [[Jedi Order]] during the [[High Republic Era]]. She served as a [[diplomat]] between the [[Baran Do Sages]] and the [[Jedi]] Order. The sages specialized in [[precognition]], but were unable to grasp a clear [[Force vision|vision]] of Paan's future, which worried them.<ref name="VG" /> In [[132 BBY]],<ref name="Death" /> Paan joined [[Jedi Master]] [[Sol]] and a [[Khofar Jedi task force|group]] of Jedi,<ref name="Day">{{Acolyte|Day (episode)}}</ref> organized by Jedi Master [[Veo Holden]], to [[Mission to Khofar|locate]] the [[assassin]] [[Mae-ho Aniseya]] and [[Prisoner|arrest]] her on<ref name="VG" /> the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]]<ref name=Revenge Justice">{{Acolyte|Revenge / Justice}}</ref> [[planet]]<ref name="VG" /> [[Khofar]] before she could [[Death|kill]] the secluded Jedi Master [[Kelnacca]]. Jedi Knight [[Yord Fandar]] briefed the Jedi group aboard a [[Polan-717 Jedi transport]] en route to Khofar. Upon arrival, she waited at a camp with the other Jedi while the [[Padawan]] [[Jecki Lon]] communicated with [[Taibik Kajok|some]] [[Wiltoo Kajok|locals]] on Kelnacca's whereabouts. After the team received word of Kelnacca entering the nearby [[forest]], the [[Tynnan]] [[Bazil]] led the expedition while following Kelnacca's scent. At [[Local day|nightfall]], the group arrived at [[Kelnacca's shelter]] and fanned out around its entrance.<ref name="Day" />

[[File:KhofarMissionJedi-OfficialAcolyteX.png|thumb|left|225px|Ithia Paan (far right) stands with her fellow Jedi against "the Stranger."]]
As the [[Sith]] practitioner known as "[[the Stranger]]" approached the group from behind, Paan and the others turned to observe him. After the Sith ignited his [[The Stranger's lightsaber|lightsaber]], Paan ignited her [[lightsaber]] and charged at the Stranger alongside the other Jedi, only for the Sith to [[Force push|knock]] the group away [[Force power|with]] [[the Force]].<ref name="Day" /> After the Jedi [[Lightsaber combat|reengaged]] the Sith, the Stranger knocked Paan to her knees before impaling the Kel Dor through her chest. Paan<ref name="Night">{{Acolyte|Night}}</ref> groaned<ref name="Night Sub">{{Acolyte|Night}} {{Subtitles|Disney+}}</ref> as she died.<ref name="Death" /> Later, [[Vernestra Rwoh]] and another group of Jedi arrived on Khofar to investigate the Jedi [[task force]]'s defeat. Upon finding and investigating the bodies of Paan and her companions, Rwoh informed fellow Jedi [[Mog Adana]] that the bodies needed to be prepared for [[burial]].<ref name="Teach">{{Acolyte|Teach / Corrupt}}</ref> Paan's death was catalogued as part of the Khofar mission while other details were locked away and intentionally misreported by Rwoh.<ref name="VG" />

==Personality and traits==
Ithia Paan was a [[Gender|female]]<ref name="Trivia" /> Kel Dor with [[Color|brown]] skin.<ref name="VG" />

==Powers and abilities==
Paan was [[Force-sensitive]] and was capable of precognition, though her foresight was no more accurate than that of other Jedi Knights with the same amount of [[Jedi training|training]].<ref name="VG" /> She was capable of [[Lightsaber duel|dueling]] with lightsabers.<ref name="Night" />

==Equipment==
Paan's [[Mission robes|Jedi apparel]] consisted of brown [[robe]]s with gold [[clothing]] underneath. She also wore a brown [[belt]].<ref name="VG" /> Her lightsaber featured a single green blade.<ref name="Day" /> Paan wore a black [[antiox breath mask]] to protect her [[lung]]s from [[oxygen]],<ref name="VG" /> which was toxic to Kel Dor.<ref name="HC">{{HelmetCollectionCite|32|Databank A-Z}}</ref> She also had a pair of black [[goggles]]<ref name="VG" /> to prevent her [[eye]]s from drying out.<ref name="HC" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Beyond grateful to have had the chance to play a Jedi!|Katie McDonnell, on potraying Ithia Paan|<ref name="McDonnell">{{Instagram|username=katiemcdonnell|url=p/C8sMfS8NiXG|author=[[Katie McDonnell]]|date=2024-06-26|quote=Beyond grateful to have had the chance to play a Jedi! 🙏🏼&hellip;And only slightly offended that out of all the stunt Jedi, they chose to hide my face. 😅#theacolyte #starwars #ithiapaan #keldor #jedi|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/8Acgl|archivefile=File:KatieMcDonnell-IthiaPaan-Instagram.png}}</ref>}}
Ithia Paan first appeared, albeit unidentified, in "[[Day (episode)|Day]],"<ref name="Day" /> the fourth episode of the live action [[Disney+]] television series ''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte]]'', which aired on [[June 18]], [[2024]].<ref name="EPG">{{SW|url=series/the-acolyte/season-1-episode-4-day-episode-guide|text="Day" Episode Guide &#124; The Acolyte}}</ref> The Kel Dor was first previewed in a [[Celebration Europe (2023)|Celebration Europe]]-exclusive trailer<ref name="CelebrationTrailer">{{CelebrationTrailer|''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte]]''|Celebration Europe (2023)}}</ref> released during the [[Lucasfilm]] Studio Showcase on [[April 7]], [[2023]].<ref name="Showcase">{{SW|url=news/swce-2023-lucasfilm-studio-showcase|text=SWCE 2023: 11 Highlights from Lucasfilm's Studio Showcase|date=2023-04-08}}</ref> Paan was identified the [[June 19|day]] after the episode's airing by the official ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[Wikipedia:Twitter|Twitter]] account, after a fan inquired about the character's name.<ref name="Name">{{Twitter|username=starwars|url=status/1803241203531763794|name=[[Star Wars]]|date=2024-06-19|quote=name's Ithia Paan, sorry! #TheAcolyte|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/OLje8|archivefile=File:StarWars-IthiaPaan-Twitter.png}}</ref> She was portrayed onscreen by stunt performer [[Katie McDonnell]],<ref name="McDonnell" /> though she was only credited as a stunt performer.<ref name="Day" /><ref name="Night" /> McDonnell was grateful to play a Jedi and joked she was offended only her face was covered among the Jedi task force.<ref name="McDonnell" />

[[File:IthiaPaanRender-TheArtOfTheAcolyte.png|thumb|right|200px|The render of Ithia Paan by Louis Wiltshire]]
[[Leslye Headland]], executive producer of ''The Acolyte'', personally choose the color of the show's original characters' lightsabers<ref name="Color">{{OfficialYouTube|channel=@RottenTomatoesTV|name=Rotten Tomatoes|link=Wikipedia:Rotten Tomatoes|video=hkJos35CuV0|text='The Acolyte' Cast on New Lightsabers and Droids|date=2024-05-30}}</ref>&mdash;which included Ithia Paan and her lightsaber<ref name="Day" />&mdash;based on the aesthetics of their scenes and personalities.<ref name="Color" /> The shots of Khofar for the Jedi task force landing and walking were filmed in the National Park Fanal of [[Wikipedia:Madeira|Madeira]] while the scenes inside the forest and at Kelnacca's shelter were filmed at [[Shinfield Studios]] in [[Wikipedia:Reading, Berkshire|Reading]],<ref name="Fantha">{{WebCite|url=https://www.fanthatracks.com/news/the-acolyte-a-journey-to-the-filming-locations-part-1-madeira|text=The Acolyte: A journey to the filming locations Part 1: Madeira|author=[[Sander de Lange|de Lange, Sander]]|date=2024-08-24|work=[https://www.fanthatracks.com Fantha Tracks]|archivedate=20241204220147}}</ref> [[Wikipedia:England|England]].<ref name="England">{{Lucasfilm|url=news/julian-foddy-acolyte|text=Visual Effects Supervisor Julian Foddy Talks World-Building ''The Acolyte''|author=[[Lucas O. Seastrom|Seastrom, Lucas O.]]|date=2024-07-31}}</ref> During production, Paan was referred to as "Not Plo Koon," which was a reference to [[Plo Koon]]<ref name="ArtOf">''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Acolyte]]''</ref>&mdash;a Kel Dor Jedi Master on the [[Jedi Council]] during the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="SWE">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref> Changes were made to established traits of Kel Dor, including the eye shapes, to give Paan "femininity." [[Louis Wiltshire]], creature concept designer and senior sculpture for the series, created a render of the Kel Dor, which was included in the<ref name="ArtOf" /> [[2026]]<ref name="ArtOfRelease">{{Abrams|url=product/art-of-star-wars-the-acolyte_9781419777349|text=The Art of Star Wars: The Acolyte}}</ref> reference book ''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Acolyte]]'' written by [[Kristin Baver]].<ref name="ArtOf" /> [[Brian Best]],<ref name="BrianInstagram">{{Instagram|username=brianbestfx|url=p/DCK9owaK860|name=[[Brian Best]]|date=2024-11-11|archiveurl=https://archive.is/wip/lt3On}}</ref> a senior modeller for ''The Acolyte'',<ref name="Day" /> created a mold for Ithia Paan during production.<ref name="BrianInstagram" /> [[Neal Scanlan]], creature and droid special effects creative supervisor for the series, called Paan's design "beautiful."<ref name="ArtOf" />

